us pathogenesis</article-title><source>Virology</source><volume>344</volume><fpage>9</fpage><lpage>16</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16364730</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030109-b013"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lefeuvre</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Marianneau</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Deubel</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Current assessment of yellow fever and yellow fever vaccine</article-title><source>Curr Infect Dis Rep</source><volume>6</volume><fpage>96</fpage><lpage>104</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15023271</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030109-b014"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pulendran</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahmed</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Translating innate immunity into immunological memory: Implications for vaccine development</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>124</volume><fpage>849</fpage><lpage>863</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16497593</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030109-b015"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haller</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Kochs</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Weber</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>The interferon response circuit: Induction and suppression by pathogenic viruses</article-title><source>Virology</source><volume>344</volume><fpage>119</fpage><lpage>130</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16364743</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030109-b016"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Richt</surname><give